<!DOCTYPE html>
@* lang follows the request culture; a hardcoded "en" mislabels every
   Vietnamese page for screen readers and translation tools. *@
<html lang="@System.Globalization.CultureInfo.CurrentUICulture.TwoLetterISOLanguageName" data-theme="grunge-light">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <meta name="description" content="QuickShareCloud — secure temporary file sharing with auto-expiry." />
    <title>QuickShareCloud</title>

    <meta name="color-scheme" content="light" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#EDE9DC" />
    <base href="/" />

    @* PWA (issue #14): installable shell + Android Web Share Target *@
    <link rel="manifest" href="/manifest.webmanifest" />

    @* Bricolage Grotesque (display) + Archivo (UI/body) + Courier Prime (labels, codes, measurements).
       All three are SIL OFL — chosen for legibility and license safety. *@
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Bricolage+Grotesque:opsz,wght@12..96,400..800&family=Archivo:wght@400..800&family=Courier+Prime:wght@400;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />

    @* DAUB anti-FOUC: set theme before CSS loads *@
    <script>
        (function() {
            try {
                var family = window.localStorage.getItem('db-family') || 'grunge';
                var scheme = window.localStorage.getItem('db-scheme') || 'light';
                // Map family+scheme to theme variant
                var familyMap = {
                    grunge: { dark: 'grunge-dark', light: 'grunge-light' },
                    default: { dark: 'dark', light: 'light' },
                    solarized: { dark: 'solarized-dark', light: 'solarized' },
                    ink: { dark: 'ink', light: 'ink-light' },
                    ember: { dark: 'ember', light: 'ember-light' },
                    bone: { dark: 'bone-dark', light: 'bone' }
                };
                var theme = (familyMap[family] && familyMap[family][scheme]) || 'grunge-light';
                document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', theme);
            } catch (e) {}
        })();
    </script>

    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/QuickShare.styles.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://daub.dev/daub.css" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/app.css" />

    @* HTMX head outlet for enhanced navigation *@
    <HtmxHeadOutlet />
    <HeadOutlet />
</head>
<body>
<!--
DIRECTION CONTRACT · seed ad3dafb6
THESIS: Every delivery is a card in your stack; sending a file is flipping a card. Refuses both
the category's floating white card on a soft gradient and minimal flat-tech.
OWN-WORLD: Colorized classic-Mac / HyperCard grammar: putty dither ground, white cards with 2px
ink borders and hard offset shadows, striped title bars, a double-ring default button, drawn
pixel iconography. Six Apple colors rationed by role — blue wash is active, the rainbow is
progress and nothing else, yellow is an accent fill never type on paper.
STORY: A Vietnamese sender sees at once: drop a file, get a link, share it on Zalo — no account,
end-to-end encrypted, server cannot read it.
FIRST VIEWPORT: Menu-bar navbar; the page as a white card on the dithered desktop; display voice
Bricolage Grotesque 800, facts in Courier Prime; the primary action wears the default-button ring.
FORM: HyperCard Stack — user-pinned challenger ("thêm nhiều màu"); roll ad3dafb6.
FINISH: unreviewed and undocumented is unfinished; this build ends with the finish review, the verdict, and DESIGN.md
-->
    <Routes />

    <script src="https://daub.dev/daub.js"></script>
    <script>
        // Set grunge theme family (defaults to the light sheet)
        (function() {
            if (window.DAUB) {
                var family = window.localStorage.getItem('db-family') || 'grunge';
                var scheme = window.localStorage.getItem('db-scheme') || 'light';
                window.DAUB.setFamily(family);
                window.DAUB.setScheme(scheme);
            }
        })();
    </script>
    <script src="/js/client-error-reporting.js" asp-append-version="true"></script>
    <script src="/js/ad-component.js" asp-append-version="true"></script>
    <script src="/lib/qrcode/qrcode.min.js"></script>
    <script defer src="/lib/alpinejs/cdn.min.js" asp-append-version="true"></script>
    <script>
        // PWA (issue #14): progressive enhancement — a SW failure must never
        // break the page.
        if ('serviceWorker' in navigator) {
            window.addEventListener('load', function () {
                navigator.serviceWorker.register('/sw.js').catch(function () { });
            });
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>
